From bb0f9b90a31a7e559c3418273568bafc00efcdc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 05:05:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 562/638] aros: route malloc through the PartitionAlloc
 allocator shim

Chromium's non-Blink allocations went to stdc.library's single
semaphore-protected pool, so every malloc/free across the ~40 runtime threads
serialised on one lock (six threads waiting on it at a time in the hosted
probes). Enable the allocator shim with PartitionAlloc as malloc, as on Linux.

stdc.library still allocates on the program's behalf (strdup, asprintf,
realpath, scandir), so free()/realloc() route pointers PartitionAlloc does not
manage back to the library through its jump table. Thread caches use pthread
keys: thread_local is emulated on AROS and allocates on first access.

The Exec API macros clash with PartitionAlloc identifiers now that the
starscan headers reach platform_thread_posix.cc, so they are included last.
